    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS OF AMERICAN AIRLINES, INC."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 28,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 13.0, 730.667, 580.667, 778.0 ],
    "font" : "DejaVuSans",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "The Treasury Loan Warrants do not have any voting rights and are freely transferrable, with registration rights. Each Treasury Loan Warrant expires on the fifth anniversary of the date of issuance of such Treasury Loan Warrant. The Treasury Loan Warrants will be exercisable either through net share settlement or cash, at AAG's option. The Treasury Loan Warrants were issued solely as compensation to the U.S. Government related to entry into the Treasury Loan Agreement. No separate proceeds were received upon issuance of the Treasury Loan Warrants or will be received upon exercise thereof."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 29,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 23.0, 709.667, 188.667, 722.0 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "DejaVuSans-BoldOblique",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "(c) Recent Accounting Pronouncement"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 30,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 24.0, 698.667, 288.0, 707.333 ],
    "font" : "DejaVuSans-Oblique",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "ASU 2016-13: Measurement of Credit Losses on Financial Instruments"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 31,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 13.0, 647.667, 581.333, 695.333 ],
    "font" : "DejaVuSans",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "This ASU requires the use of an expected loss model for certain types of financial instruments and requires consideration of a broader range of reasonable and supportable information to calculate credit loss estimates. For trade receivables, loans and held-to-maturity debt securities, an estimate of lifetime expected credit losses is required. For available-for-sale debt securities, an allowance for credit losses will be required rather than a reduction to the carrying value of the asset. American adopted this accounting standard prospectively as of January 1, 2020, and it did not have a material impact on American's consolidated financial statements."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 32,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 24.0, 628.667, 142.0, 638.0 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "DejaVuSans-BoldOblique",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "(d) Short-term Investments"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 33,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 12.667, 580.0, 581.0, 626.0 ],
    "font" : "DejaVuSans",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Short-term investments are classified as available-for-sale and stated at fair value. Realized gains and losses are recorded in nonoperating expense on American’s consolidated statements of operations. Unrealized gains and losses are recorded in accumulated other comprehensive loss on American’s consolidated balance sheets. For investments in an unrealized loss position, American determines whether a credit loss exists by considering information about the collectability of the instrument, current market conditions and reasonable and supportable forecasts of economic conditions. There have been no credit losses."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 34,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 24.0, 559.333, 228.667, 569.333 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "DejaVuSans-BoldOblique",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "(e) Restricted Cash and Short-term Investments"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 35,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 13.333, 536.667, 581.333, 557.667 ],
    "font" : "DejaVuSans",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "American has restricted cash and short-term investments related primarily to money market funds to be used to finance a substantial portion of the cost of the renovation and expansion of Terminal 8 at JFK and collateral held to support workers’ compensation obligations."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 36,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 23.333, 517.333, 224.0, 527.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "DejaVuSans-BoldOblique",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "(f) Aircraft Fuel, Spare Parts and Supplies, Net"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 37,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 13.333, 495.333, 578.667, 514.667 ],
    "font" : "DejaVuSans",
    "font size" : 7.492,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Aircraft fuel is recorded on a first-in, first-out basis. Spare parts and supplies are recorded at average costs less an allowance for obsolescence. These items are expensed when used."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
